      "standardized_narrative": "The syndicate reported a net prior year reserve release of $128.216 million for 2024, representing 7.68% of its opening gross claims outstanding. This release was primarily driven by favorable claims development in the International Casualty, Motor, and Property Treaty books, which benefited from reductions in prior years' loss estimates. However, some areas experienced adverse development, notably in US Casualty, where further strengthening was required in parts of the portfolio due to social and economic inflationary pressures, litigation severity, and claims volatility. Additionally, Faraday's Aviation book saw adverse experience and increased cost reserves related to Russia/Ukraine litigations. The overall movement is a mix of releases and strengthenings across different lines of business.",
      "raw_causal_phrases": [
        "prior year loss experience developing broadly in line with our best estimate expectations in most segments",
        "claims costs, due to general and social inflationary pressures and litigation severity in particular, are continuing to offset these improvements",
        "revisions to the underlying original pricing assumptions and reserving bases",
        "further reserve strengthening in some parts of the portfolio to address claims volatility and development concerns and recent loss experience",
        "Faraday's Aviation book suffered adverse experience in 2024 due losses and increasing the cost reserves for Russia / Ukraine related litigations",
        "International Casualty and Motor books were profitable benefitting from favourable prior year developments",
        "recent increase in the UK Personal Injury Discount Rate",
        "latest 2024 Annual Survey of Hours and Earnings (ASHE) which has decreased from the heightened UK inflation in 2023 but remains elevated by historical standards"
